{"title":"1964 IMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems of the 6th <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO\">IMO</a> 1964 in USSR.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_I\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day I</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_II\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day II</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Resources\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Resources</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_I\">Day I</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day I\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>(a) Find all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/0/4b063495d0243e7bc52c3a7f231362bdc4a03775.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>(b) Prove that there is no positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/8/fb810ba5d07f7078bea65c2ae90edf15e09874f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1964 IMO Problems/Problem 1\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc6d9a6172d35127b6cb37ea92192caf7029a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> are the sides of a triangle. Prove that \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/8/2c8afb405fe890dd89759ea3a2ed2e527038adfc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2(b+c-a)+b^2(c+a-b)+c^2(a+b-c)\\le{3abc}.\\]\" width=\"405\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1964 IMO Problems/Problem 2\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>A circle is inscribed in a triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> with sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />. Tangents to the circle parallel to the sides of the triangle are contructed. Each of these tangents cuts off a triangle from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. In each of these triangles, a circle is inscribed. Find the sum of the areas of all four inscribed circles (in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />).\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1964 IMO Problems/Problem 3\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_II\">Day II</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day II\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Seventeen people correspond by mail with one another - each one with all\nthe rest. In their letters only three different topics are discussed. Each pair\nof correspondents deals with only one of these topics. Prove that there are\nat least three people who write to each other about the same topic.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1964 IMO Problems/Problem 4\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Suppose five points in a plane are situated so that no two of the straight lines\njoining them are parallel, perpendicular, or coincident. From each point perpendiculars\nare drawn to all the lines joining the other four points. Determine\nthe maximum number of intersections that these perpendiculars can have.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1964 IMO Problems/Problem 5\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>In tetrahedron <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is connected with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28ef8b28c502478e0c30de8cfc0f0102c5c7cd70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" />, the centroid of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. Lines parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/6/a86e2cb929814ee4ea3b40ee3adf380e84686710.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DD_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"17\" /> are drawn through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f642cbbd390b4882363ab6b5c2906dbf6be6cc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. These lines intersect the planes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/7/d075c845f64c275c2df875b5fef4c9cd74b6cb56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCD, CAD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6adfd3ad27a2dddeb0af7131d73c33c86991e93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> in points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/b/20b5016493b0d7c21d955a96116263208b10c8a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1, B_1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b97eb4ad6e4e7a5a97e2547d9ed6e965960d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />, respectively. Prove that the volume of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is one third the volume of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa4367e81390a69cde1e059f6edd553dd386e40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1B_1C_1D_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"17\" />. Is the result true if point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/f/e8f92a2dbe00dd92d8b0d4ddd8cda7c1010cc6a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_o$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> is selected anywhere within <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1964 IMO Problems/Problem 6\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO\" title=\"1964 IMO\">1964 IMO</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=1&amp;cid=16&amp;year=1964\">IMO 1964 Problems on the Resources page</a></li></ul>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\">IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO\" title=\"1964 IMO\">1964 IMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_IMO\" title=\"1963 IMO\">1963 IMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1964 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1964 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1964 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1964 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1964 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1964 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_IMO\" title=\"1965 IMO\">1965 IMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018041802\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.027 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.042 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 190/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 836/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 56/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4743/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.645      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.645      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:8263:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018041802 and revision id 143746. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}